; Two SplitVectorize nodes share the same first (PHI) part: the bundle
; <%ph0, %ph1, %ph0, %ph1>. The first node builds it as a real PHI node entry,
; so its reuse shuffle is emitted at getFirstInsertionPt(), i.e. it becomes the
; first non-PHI instruction of %bb. The second node reuses that entry through a
; gather sub-node, but setInsertPointAfterBundle() still takes the IsPHI path
; and resets the insert point to getFirstNonPHIIt() - which is now the reuse
; shuffle itself. Check that the insert point of the split node is advanced past
; the vector values, reused by its operands, i.e. all the shuffles are emitted
; after the values they consume:
;   Instruction does not dominate all uses!
;     %9 = shufflevector <2 x float> %4, <2 x float> poison, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 1, i32 0, i32 1>
;     %5 = shufflevector <4 x float> %9, <4 x float> poison, <4 x i32> <i32 0, i32 1, i32 0, i32 1>

